no_prelude

# The explicit opt-out (docs/prelude-scope-v0.md §4.2 step 5). With the prelude
# unconditional, a file that genuinely wants to be preludeless — a codegen fixture
# exercising a path where no typeclass dict witness is in scope, say — says so here
# rather than achieving it accidentally by declaring no imports.
#
# `no_prelude` is a HEADER directive: source.strip_headers removes it before the
# lexer runs, so it needs no grammar support. `print` is special-cased in the
# compiler rather than declared in the prelude, which is what lets a preludeless
# file produce output at all.

fn twice(n: Int) -> Int = n + n

fn main() -> Unit !{IO} =
  print(twice(21))
